                <pb facs="0704" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg693"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123EN3/523: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-04T15:00:00-05:00">March 4, 1937—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>68. Engert is departing from Addis Ababa on March 5 and instructions have been
                    issued to close the office entirely on March 31. Unless you perceive some
                    objection please advise the Foreign Office orally and informally that we should
                    be appreciative if it would continue to furnish us, as has been done during
                    recent months, with any available information regarding welfare of American
                    nationals in Ethiopia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
